Aim

To familiarize ourselves with the general breadboard and its connections.

Apparatus

Breadboard, jumper wires, +5V DC supply, LEDs and resistors.

Procedure

1. Identify the power rails and terminal strips of the breadboard.


2. Connect +5V and GND to the power rails.


3. Connect the power rails using jumper wires if required.


4. Place the components on the breadboard.


5. Make series and parallel connections according to the circuit.


6. Check the connections.


7. Observe the LED operation.



Virtual Labs specifically describes the breadboard as a solderless board and explains its power-rail and terminal-strip connections. 

Important Points

Breadboard is used for temporary/prototype circuits.

No soldering is required.

Power rails are used for power supply.

Terminal strips are used to connect components.

The centre gap separates the two sides.
Result

The basic construction and connections of a general breadboard were successfully studied.
